# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BrowserLink — share Hermes's agent browser with a human viewer (P2P WebRTC)
# Repo: https://github.com/MrBenJ/hermes-browserlink  (see INSTALL.md §4)
#
# What this is: BrowserLink is an unpacked MV3 Chrome extension loaded into
# the Chromium that Hermes drives. It lets the agent host a tab over WebRTC
# so a human can open a viewer link, finish one blocked step (login, 2FA,
# CAPTCHA) and leave, without handing the agent any credentials. The lines
# below make Hermes launch that Chromium headed and with the extension loaded.
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Install the extension to a durable path first (INSTALL.md §3), e.g.
#      <HERMES_HOME>/browser-extensions/browserlink
#   2. Replace every /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/HERMES_HOME below with the absolute
#      path of your Hermes home (usually ~/.hermes, or $HERMES_HOME if set),
#      written out in full, e.g. /home/alice/.hermes or /Users/alice/.hermes.
#      INSTALL.md §4.2 has a one-liner that prints the filled-in block.
#   3. Back up your Hermes .env, then paste this block into it. If the .env
#      already sets AGENT_BROWSER_ARGS, do NOT add a second line: merge per
#      the rules in INSTALL.md §4.3 (keep every existing flag, never add a
#      duplicate --load-extension / --disable-extensions-except).
#   4. Restart Hermes fully (see below).
#
# Read once at Hermes start: .env is loaded when the gateway starts, so any
# change here needs a full Hermes/gateway restart, not just a new browser tab.
#
# Rollback: restore the backup (or delete this whole block), then restart
# Hermes. Nothing else on the system is changed by these lines.
#
# Privacy note: when a viewer asks the host to navigate / open / switch to a
# site, BrowserLink resolves that hostname over DNS-over-HTTPS to Cloudflare
# (cloudflare-dns.com) to refuse names that point at loopback/LAN/private
# addresses. Only those hostnames are sent (no paths, no cookies). If the
# lookup fails, the request is refused (fails closed). MV3 extensions have no
# DNS API, which is why this goes over DoH. See README "What the link
# actually grants".
#
# Headed: MV3 extensions don't load in Chromium's headless shell, and Hermes
# launches headless by default. Without this the extension silently never
# loads (INSTALL.md §4.1).
AGENT_BROWSER_HEADED=true
#
# Chromium flags. Format rules for this value:
#   - comma-separated, no spaces around commas, no quotes
#   - absolute paths only: .env does NOT expand ~ or $HOME here
# Flags:
#   --load-extension=<dir>            : load the unpacked BrowserLink extension
#   --disable-extensions-except=<dir> : load ONLY BrowserLink, no other
#                                       extensions (keeps the profile clean)
#   --disable-backgrounding-occluded-windows : keep streaming frames when the
#     browser window is hidden, minimised or covered. Without it Chromium
#     may throttle occluded windows and the viewer can stall. Side effect:
#     the window keeps rendering while hidden, which costs extra CPU/GPU.
# Linux/Docker: setting AGENT_BROWSER_ARGS turns off Hermes's automatic
# --no-sandbox,--disable-dev-shm-usage. If Hermes runs as root or in Docker,
# append those two flags too (INSTALL.md §4.3).
AGENT_BROWSER_ARGS=--load-extension=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/HERMES_HOME/browser-extensions/browserlink,--disable-extensions-except=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/HERMES_HOME/browser-extensions/browserlink,--disable-backgrounding-occluded-windows
# --- end BrowserLink -------------------------------------------------------
